The workflow at `.github/workflows/rill-quality.yml` executes actual
product-source quality checks. Missing scripts, absent tests, incompatible
dependency locks, analyzer errors and insecure dependencies **fail**.
Do not weaken existing checks or claim fixtures as production evidence.

{% if react %}
### Mandatory React product contracts

At `[[ react_root ]]`: committed application source in
`[[ react_sources ]]` and actual component/unit/integration test
files. Native CI invokes Biome, TypeScript, Vitest with a reviewed
source-coverage threshold, Playwright `@e2e` and `@a11y`
real Chrome scenarios directly. The product's native `build` script
must produce its actual deployment artifact. Do not replace a native
tool with green shell-echo scripts or skip component/API failure paths.
The Playwright project must be named `chrome` with
`use: { channel: "chrome" }`; generated CI selects that specific
project. The build must freshly emit `[[ react_build_artifact ]]`.
Never use downloaded Chromium in place of system Google Chrome.
{% endif %}
{% if node %}
### Mandatory Node product contracts

At `[[ node_root ]]`: committed application source in
`[[ node_sources ]]` and real unit and integration tests. Native
CI invokes Biome, TypeScript and selected
`[[ node_test_runner ]]` runner with source coverage thresholds.
The product's real `build` script remains mandatory and must
produce the deployable package. Check HTTP/contract/service behavior,
negative cases and recovery. No-op test scripts cannot replace
native source checks. The Node `node:test` profile requires
a locked `c8@12.0.0` development dependency. `c8 --all` checks
unloaded source files against the per-file coverage floor.
The build must freshly emit `[[ node_build_artifact ]]`.
{% endif %}
{% if python %}
### Python quality contracts

Locked uv project includes Ruff, mypy, pytest/pytest-cov,
`pip-licenses` and the application dependencies. The PEP 517 build
backend must be pinned in `[build-system]` **and** installed as a
locked dev dependency: `uv build --no-build-isolation` deliberately
fails when that backend is missing instead of resolving a new version.
Static checks, unit/integration tests, coverage and build must pass.
{% endif %}
{% if shell %}
### Shell quality contracts

ShellCheck and shfmt audit `.sh` and extensionless Bash/sh shebang
scripts from one inventory. Bats tests real executable behavior.
Missing source and tests are errors, not an implicit skip.
{% endif %}

